Subject: [PATCH] qemu: use TCG on Windows until the bundled WHPX is fixed

QEMU 11.1.0 can fail to initialize WHPX on supported Windows 11 hosts with
`failed to initialize whpx: Invalid argument`. Use software emulation until
the bundled QEMU is upgraded so the environment remains usable.

---
 pkg/driver/qemu/qemu.go | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pkg/driver/qemu/qemu.go b/pkg/driver/qemu/qemu.go
--- a/pkg/driver/qemu/qemu.go
+++ b/pkg/driver/qemu/qemu.go
@@ -1228,7 +1228,11 @@
 			return "nvmm"
 		case "windows":
-			return "whpx"
+			// QEMU 11.1.0's WHPX path fails with
+			// "failed to initialize whpx: Invalid argument" on supported
+			// Windows 11 hosts. Use TCG until the bundled QEMU is upgraded;
+			// a slow VM is preferable to an environment that cannot start.
+			logrus.Warn("WHPX is disabled for Windows until the bundled QEMU is upgraded; using TCG")
+			return "tcg"
 		}
